#==============================================================================================
#
#   script - The Script node's API: Houdini's Python SOP, in Luce Base
#
#   DESCRIPTION:
#       A Script node's code is a whole Base module with `pub func cook(k: Cook*) -> !`.
#       luced-3d builds it with the real compiler into a small tool that imports this
#       module, and runs it in a child process: the generated `main` calls `serve`, which
#       takes one cook request, loads the inputs, runs `cook` and writes the result.
#
#       `Geometry` is a geometry set opened for editing: points, polygons, attributes and
#       groups through an edit form of its mesh (columns that grow as elements are added),
#       curves, point clouds, instances and detail attributes through the set. `Verb` runs
#       any verb of the node menu by name. `Cook` (the `k` of the code) holds the inputs,
#       the spare parameters, the timeline and the console.
#
#       The parent side (`ScriptProcess`, `ScriptText`) is here too: it starts the tool,
#       sends a request and reads the replies, so both ends of the protocol live together.
#
#==============================================================================================
